s Compensation and Classification Recruitment Total Rewards Institutional Equity and Diversity Ethics and Compliance Policies, Forms, Contracts Calendar Schedule Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Announcements Human Resources Staff OneHR Customer Service Center Jobs, Careers and Compensation Considering a position at William Paterson University? If so, you are choosing to work with a vibrant, diverse, inclusive and welcoming community of Pioneers who value and recognize continuous learning, growth and contribution to the achievement of the University’s Strategic Goals. The University is designated as a Hispanic-serving institution, and has been honored with the status of being designated as a Military Friendly® School for 11 consecutive years. The University is committed to your continuous learning and development as you are a valued member of our community. That commitment to developing human capital is demonstrated through the broad array of resources available to help you learn, grow and develop the skills needed to position yourself for career advancement opportunities which may arise. These resources are both self-paced and employer driven. Opportunities are available through the following venues: EAP – Training Center Vector Solutions (Safe Colleges) Additionally, we encourage you to review job postings regularly through our Talent Management Portal where employment opportunities are found. The William Paterson University of New Jersey is committed to equal employment opportunity and to maintaining an academic and work environment for students, faculty and staff which is conducive to the achievement of educational and career goals on the basis of ability and performance, and which is free of discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, national origin, nationality, ancestry, sex/gender (including pregnancy), affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, civil union status, domestic partnership status, familial status, religion, atypical hereditary cellular or blood trait, genetic information, liability for service in the Armed Forces of the United States, or disability, except where a particular qualification is specifically permitted and is essential to successful job performance . Prospective Employees Newly Hired Employees Current Employees - Resources Request Info Visit Apply Quick Links Employment Opportunities Campus Map Contact Us Get Connected Event Calendar WP News Give to William Paterson Social Media Directory WP Connect 300 Pompton Road | Wayne, New Jersey 07470 (973) 720-2000 Copyright © 2026 | Privacy Policy"
