le Bus Schedules [pdf] Resources Division of Student Development Student Handbook (policies and resources) University Bookstore Other Departments Website Comments Equity & Inclusion Division of Equity and Inclusion Office for Student Diversity and Inclusion Services Accessibility Resource Center (Disability Services) Career Development Child Development Center Dean of Students Events and Conference Services Student Accounts (Bursar) Student Enrollment Services Veteran/Military Services Health & Safety University Police Rave Guardian Mobile App Counseling, Health, & Wellness Center Safe Walk Escort Service About Us What's Happening University News Events Calendar Arts on Campus Social Media Directory Community Child Development Center Civic Engagement Consumer Information Employment Opportunities Hispanic-Serving Institution Our Community University Police University Sustainability About WP All Departments University Facts Our History Our Background Mission, Vision, and Core Values Honors and Awards University Annual Report Student Achievements University Virtual Tour Our Alumni Giving to WP University Policies Open Public Records Request Strategic Plan Equity & Inclusion Division of Equity and Inclusion Office for Student Diversity and Inclusion Administration Board of Trustees Office of the President Provost and Academic Affairs Administration, Capital Planning, and Physical Plant Operations Enrollment Management Equity and Inclusion Finance and Controller General Counsel Human Resources Information Technology Institutional Advancement Marketing and Public Relations Strategic Initiatives and University Relations Student Development Athletics Cultural Events WP connect Maps & Contact Give Apply INFORMATION FOR Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Donors Alumni Our Local Community What is your First Destination After Graduation? Complete your Graduate Survey on Handshake. Connect to Handshake Career Development Center About Us Get Career Ready: Career Resources Career Prep & Resources PowerPaths: Career Experience Program Your Student Success Plan Pioneer to Professional Blog Forage Gain Experience: Jobs & Internships Career Communities Career & Professional Success Badge Career Closet Recruit at WP Faculty & Staff Partners Pesce Family Mentoring Institute Career Events Career Development Center Getting you ready for the workforce From exploring majors to career coaching and internships, the Career Development Center is the first stop on your journey to career success. We offer students and alumni a full suite of services that help you prepare for the next step—and every step beyond. Alumni Careers by the numbers $ 65,049 average starting salary for a WP grad, outpacing national average for public institutions WP alums employed or in graduate school within 6 months of graduation 40,000 Jobs/internships available via the WP Handshake job portal 120,000 Employer partners actively recruiting WP students/alumni Contact Us Career Development Center Student Center 301 300 Pompton Road Wayne, NJ 07470 Phone: 973.720.3291 Fax: 973.720.2074 Our office is open Monday - Friday from 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. To meet with a member of our staff please schedule an appointment on Navigate , or contact the Main Office at 973.720.3291 or CareerDevelopment@Wpunj.edu We're here to help In addition to a variety of Career Workshops , Employer Information Sessions , Career Fairs , and Career Coaching Sessions each semester, we offer services designed to support individual student and alumni needs. Connect with Us on the WP Handshake Career Portal Explore your Interests, Find your Path with WP Career Communities Build your Skills with the Career and Professional Success Badge Apply for a Career Mentor at the Pesce Family Mentoring Institute Get Hired! Explore Jobs and Internships on Handshake Join Handshake The WP Handshake Career Portal is your one-stop shop for full-time jobs , part-time jobs , internships , events , and signing up for career communities ! Download the mobile app for iPhone and Android to receive customized, real-time listings. Join Handshake Browse Internships Career Events and Fairs Pesce Family Mentoring Institute Join the Pesce Family Mentoring Institute to be individually paired with a mentor in your professional field of interest, who can offer personal career advice and guidance! Learn more » 96% Pesce mentees from Class of 2021 in careers or grad school within 6 months Where WP Works Our alumni are making an impact in careers with local and national businesses like the ones below. * Minority and/or Women Business Enterprise (M/WBE) What Our Graduates Say \"I gained all the building blocks I needed: experience, an internship, and interview skills.\" Heather Cook ’16 Media production and public relations major, landed a full-time job at NBC Universal right out of college. Prior to graduation, she completed a production internship at Discovery Communications. Social @ Career Development Powered by Curator.io Request Info Visit Apply Quick Links Employment Opportunities Campus Map Contact Us Get Connected Event Calendar WP News Give to William Paterson Social Media Directory WP Connect 300 Pompton Road | Wayne, New Jersey 07470 (973) 720-2000 Copyright © 2026 | Privacy Policy"
    },
